3391	3568	2177	2177	she	27	" Yes , sir , but very quietly . It was to be at St. Saviour 's , near King 's Cross , and we were to have breakfast afterwards at the St. Pancras Hotel . Hosmer came for us in a hansom , but as there were two of us he put us both into it and stepped himself into a four - wheeler , which happened to be the only other cab in the street . We got to the church first , and when the four - wheeler drove up we waited for him to step out , but he never did , and when the cabman got down from the box and looked there was no one there ! The cabman said that he could not imagine what had become of him , for he had seen him get in with his own eyes . That was last Friday , Mr. Holmes , and I have never seen or heard anything since then to throw any light upon what became of him . "
